  "aboutCopyVersion": "Copy the version, for a bug report",
  "aboutPurposeTitle": "What it's for",
  "aboutPurposeBody": "DNet lets you chat, call and share files with the people around you when there is no internet, no signal and no server, or when you would rather not use them. There is no account, no number and no email: your identity is a key made on your device, and all it needs is a name.",
  "aboutAimTitle": "What it aims for",
  "aboutAimBody": "To keep people in touch when networks fail, are switched off or can't be trusted: at events, while travelling, in remote places and during outages. Private by default, owned by nobody, and open for anyone to check.",
  "aboutHowTitle": "How it works",
  "aboutHowNearbyTitle": "Finds people nearby",
  "aboutHowNearbyBody": "Devices find each other over Bluetooth and Wi-Fi, with no internet.",
  "aboutHowMeshTitle": "Passes messages along",
  "aboutHowMeshBody": "Out of range? Sealed messages hop through other DNet devices, which can't read them.",
  "aboutHowSealedTitle": "Encrypted end to end",
  "aboutHowSealedBody": "Each message is sealed on your device for the one person it's for.",
  "aboutHowSpacesTitle": "Spaces for groups",
  "aboutHowSpacesBody": "Channels and voice rooms, kept on members' devices. No server.",
  "aboutHowRadioTitle": "Long range by radio",
  "aboutHowRadioBody": "Plug in a LoRa radio to send text for kilometres, on the band that is legal where you are.",
  "aboutStatusTitle": "Where it stands",
  "aboutStatusBody": "This is an early build. It has had an internal security review but has not had an independent security review, and its Bluetooth, Wi-Fi Direct, mesh and LoRa links have not yet been verified on devices. Don't rely on it to protect anyone, or in an emergency.",
